{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295216-beastmen-and-the-effects-on-their-society","id":1295216,"title":"Beastmen and the effects on their society","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-08T22:19:29-08:00","id":1295216,"title":"Beastmen and the effects on their society","content":"So what I want to look at in this thread is the social effects of mutations on a culture.<br /> How does it change a culture when everyone has super-smell? Or spinnarets? Or poison?<br /> <br /> Mahalanka was good at this, pointing out the economic effect of Mighty Thews. But what else?<br /> <br /> So the most obvious one is wings.<br /> If everyone has wings, do you need stairs? Walls for your city? You can build a town somewhere extremely defensible.<br /> But also, think about transport. You can travel really fast... but you can't take carts with you. This encourages trade to focus on small, high-value goods.<br /> And generally, to take advantage of your flying, you probably can't use beasts of burden. That encourages society to use slaves for hard labour, but wings means your slaves are better able to escape.<br /> <br /> In warfare, you have a great advantage in intelligence-gathering, and raiding. But not much in heavy infantry, shock cavalry, or defending seized territory. <br /> This may encourage a focus on raiding, not conquest.<br /> <br /> What about other mutations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-09-2019, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:14:27-08:00","id":1295223,"title":"","content":"Well, one thing to keep in mind is that it's somewhat unlikely for a population to be <i>completely</i> made up of beastfolk. The trials to imbue the relevant mutations are risky enough that not everybody in the Lunar's dominion would be willing to risk their lives or sanity trying them. <br /> <br /> And while the mutations are hereditary, not every union will be between beastfolk. As such, I expect that some percentage of the population will remain human, no matter how many generations the Lunar keeps her beastfolk proving ground going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:31:18-08:00","id":1295226,"title":"","content":"I wonder if, over a long time, you'll get some kind of social sorting; the beastmen may all end up living in villages together, while the non-beastmen live in other villages together. Not to mention caste stratification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:31:35-08:00","id":1295227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295216-beastmen-and-the-effects-on-their-society#post1295216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what I want to look at in this thread is the social effects of mutations on a culture.<br /> How does it change a culture when everyone has super-smell? Or spinnarets? Or poison?<br /> <br /> Mahalanka was good at this, pointing out the economic effect of Mighty Thews. But what else?<br /> <br /> So the most obvious one is wings.<br /> If everyone has wings, do you need stairs? Walls for your city? You can build a town somewhere extremely defensible.<br /> But also, think about transport. You can travel really fast... but you can't take carts with you. This encourages trade to focus on small, high-value goods.<br /> And generally, to take advantage of your flying, you probably can't use beasts of burden. That encourages society to use slaves for hard labour, but wings means your slaves are better able to escape.<br /> <br /> In warfare, you have a great advantage in intelligence-gathering, and raiding. But not much in heavy infantry, shock cavalry, or defending seized territory. <br /> This may encourage a focus on raiding, not conquest.<br /> <br /> What about other mutations?</div> </div> </div> </div>How were the mutations obtained?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:35:45-08:00","id":1295228,"title":"","content":"Well there could be multiple possibilities, and that could have different effects.<br /> <br /> There's quite a lot of difference between passing Lunar trials, inheritance, and the sudden mutation of a passing wyldstorm.<br /> <br /> If you want to pick one, go for inheritance; a beastman society whose Lunar has long since passed away. But feel free to discuss any of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T03:00:56-08:00","id":1295268,"title":"","content":"I'd like to remind you of the Luthe write up; the part where it discussed the intact First Age buildings as slums because of how the mutations of most of the populace and the environment intermixed seems pertinent.<br /> <br /> Pervasive mutations can alter a society dramatically, yes, but there are other factors determining how they are used For example, if the mutations are inheirited from the culture patron/bird deity, then it might be a mark of the nobility and not utilized for 'petty things', like 'common' trade.<br /> On the other hand, if the beastfolk are a conquered people, they might serve as slaves. That might be true of wyld mutants too, especially in the aftermath of a Fair Folk raid. &quot;You are spiritually unclean and must serve your better in this life&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T03:24:29-08:00","id":1295271,"title":"","content":"Flying everywhere must be exhausting.<br /> <br /> And building places without stairs sounds unnecessarily difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T03:32:46-08:00","id":1295273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295216-beastmen-and-the-effects-on-their-society?p=1295271#post1295271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flying everywhere must be exhausting.<br /> <br /> And building places without stairs sounds unnecessarily difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... exalted. <br /> <br /> Maybe just model it as same as walking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T04:27:29-08:00","id":1295281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295216-beastmen-and-the-effects-on-their-society?p=1295271#post1295271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flying everywhere must be exhausting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. Not necessarily more so than walking. But it could be; depends a lot on the environment, thermals and so on, I expect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And building places without stairs sounds unnecessarily difficult. </div> </div> </div>Well, building a house with two floors and no stairs is easier than building one with stairs.<br /> But if your wings are too large to unfurl in, say, a crowded street, that could be an issue.<br /> And in the long run, there's issues about getting stuff up to the top floor. Furniture, for example.<br /> Not to mention the elderly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T05:09:31-08:00","id":1295284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295216-beastmen-and-the-effects-on-their-society?p=1295273#post1295273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beastfolk aren't always Exalts, though.<br /> <br /> Even for hollow-boned birds, that initial takeoff is one of the most energy-intensive expenditures an animal can make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-09-2019, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T05:43:35-08:00","id":1295290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295216-beastmen-and-the-effects-on-their-society?p=1295281#post1295281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly. Not necessarily more so than walking.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can stop walking without being dragged down by gravity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, building a house with two floors and no stairs is easier than building one with stairs. </div> </div> </div>Sure scaffolding has a part, but you can save yourself a bit of trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T09:50:37-08:00","id":1295333,"title":"","content":"I imagined a society which had humans living on the ground and Fruit Bat beastkin living in the tall, tall trees. They would trade with each other that which the others found hard to produce: metal from the humans, fruit and herbs from the bats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T12:37:24-08:00","id":1295373,"title":"","content":"Cringe worthy as it was, the 2e write-up on Ma-Ha-Suchi's Nameless Lair had the behavioral traits of the wolf-goat beastmen affect the way they interacted with First Age commodities. They refused to use the intact plumbing systems of the First Age buildings for waste disposal and instead actually ventured outside to relieve themselves due to their innate canine aversion to producing waste in the same area that they lived.<br /> <br /> Digitigrade legs are going to make using ladders and certain types of stairs more difficult, large tails interfere with sitting down and riding horses so the ergonomics of goods produced in a Lunar domain might be radically different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T08:29:20-07:00","id":1295566,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, didn't think about ergonomics. That's interesting.<br /> <br /> I'm planning a Lunar game set in the far north, and I want a few interesting beastman tribes in the PCs' area.<br /> <br /> Here are some ideas we had for beastmen in the area, can anyone think of interesting effects it'd have on their society?<br /> Gull-people<br /> Seal-people<br /> Snow hare-people<br /> Snow fox-people<br /> Beaver folk<br /> Aurochs<br /> Badgers<br /> Walrus<br /> Killer whales<br /> <br /> I was thinking that animals that live in dens might lead to a beastman group that all live underground in a series of tunnels. If they're the elite of society, it could even be that the human peasants have to live above ground where it's cold, while the elite live at the bottom, in cosy dens.<br /> Or perhaps everyone, human and beastman, live in tunnels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T08:35:59-07:00","id":1295567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295216-beastmen-and-the-effects-on-their-society?p=1295566#post1295566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, didn't think about ergonomics. That's interesting.<br /> <br /> I'm planning a Lunar game set in the far north, and I want a few interesting beastman tribes in the PCs' area.<br /> <br /> Here are some ideas we had for beastmen in the area, can anyone think of interesting effects it'd have on their society?<br /> Gull-people<br /> Seal-people<br /> Snow hare-people<br /> Snow fox-people<br /> Beaver folk<br /> Aurochs<br /> Badgers<br /> Walrus<br /> Killer whales<br /> <br /> I was thinking that animals that live in dens might lead to a beastman group that all live underground in a series of tunnels. If they're the elite of society, it could even be that the human peasants have to live above ground where it's cold, while the elite live at the bottom, in cosy dens.<br /> Or perhaps everyone, human and beastman, live in tunnels.</div> </div> </div> </div>How were the mutations obtained?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T08:58:42-07:00","id":1295570,"title":"","content":"Any method you think is interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T10:43:56-07:00","id":1295582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a hre